---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy | Relicbound"
  description="How Relicbound uses location data and protects expedition information."
>
  <article class="policy">
    <header class="page-header">
      <p class="eyebrow">Legal information</p>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="effective-date">Effective from 21 August 2026</p>
    </header>

    <section>
      <h2>Overview</h2>
      <p>
        Relicbound is designed to work without an account. The application
        does not require your name, email address or profile information.
      </p>
      <p>
        Your collection, expedition history and game progress are stored
        locally on your device.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Location data</h2>
      <p>
        Relicbound uses your device location to suggest nearby walking
        destinations, generate pedestrian routes and measure active
        expeditions.
      </p>
      <p>
        Location tracking may continue while Apple Maps is open, while
        Relicbound is running in the background or while your phone is locked
        during an active expedition.
      </p>
      <p>
        Background location tracking stops when the expedition is completed or
        abandoned.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Information stored on your device</h2>
      <p>Relicbound may store expedition summaries including:</p>

      <ul>
        <li>Destination name</li>
        <li>Approximate area</li>
        <li>Route type</li>
        <li>Distance travelled</li>
        <li>Expedition duration</li>
        <li>Completion date</li>
        <li>Recovered cases and relics</li>
      </ul>

      <p>
        Detailed GPS trails and precise starting coordinates are not retained
        after an expedition has ended.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Accounts and advertising</h2>
      <p>
        Relicbound does not require an account and does not contain
        personalised advertising.
      </p>
      <p>
        Personal information and walking history are not sold to advertisers
        or data brokers.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>The Relicbound Archive website</h2>
      <p>
        The companion website is a public product and lore archive. It does not
        receive your expedition history, collection progress or precise
        location data from the Relicbound application.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Apple Maps</h2>
      <p>
        Relicbound uses Apple Maps to search for destinations and generate
        walking directions. Your use of Apple Maps is also subject to Apple's
        own privacy policies and service terms.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Deleting your data</h2>
      <p>
        Relicbound will provide an in-app option to reset all game progress and
        locally stored expedition records.
      </p>
      <p>
        Removing the application from your device also removes its locally
        stored data, subject to any device backups managed through your Apple
        account.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        This policy may be updated when Relicbound features or data practices
        change. The effective date at the top of this page will be revised when
        an update is published.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about this privacy policy or Relicbound’s data practices can be
        sent to{" "}
        <a href="mailto:relicbound@thomaspercival.dev">
          relicbound@thomaspercival.dev
        </a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .policy {
    max-width: 48rem;
  }

  .page-header {
    width: 100%;
    min-height: auto;
    margin-bottom: clamp(4rem, 10vw, 7rem);
    padding: 0;
    display: block;
    border: 0;
  }

  .policy a {
    color: var(--colour-accent-bright);
    font-weight: 700;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }

  .policy a:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  .eyebrow {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    color: var(--colour-accent-bright);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  h1 {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .effective-date {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }

  section {
    padding-block: 2rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--colour-border);
  }

  section h2 {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 2rem);
  }

  section p:last-child,
  section ul:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  ul {
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    color: var(--colour-text-muted);
  }

  li + li {
    margin-top: 0.35rem;
  }
</style>